 Well, let=E2=80=99s see.1. =C2=A0No one is suggesting a lexed version of F=
OPL or HOIL as a language, although, as one who spoke one fairly regularly =
for thirty-some years, I can say that it is not too bad (certainly not wors=
e than Lojban in the areas both cover). =C2=A0The biggest problem is repeti=
tion, since you have to say everything the same way every time. =C2=A0So, t=
he first steps in deriving a language from =C2=A0formulae, unequivocal repe=
tition replacement: fusion and prowords, mainly. After that, the rest is ic=
ing. =C2=A0Oh, and adding a bunch of conversational expressions. =C2=A0=C2=
=A02. =C2=A0The theory goes that every sentence in any language derives by =
a series of transformations from a semantic representation, viewed as a for=
mula in an adequate HOIL. =C2=A0A correct parse, then, is one that gets bac=
k to that original formula (up to the relevant logical equivalence). Practi=
cally, this seems to mean that the derivations involved are all biunique. =
=C2=A0Of course, none of this discussion applies to Lojban, since it does n=
ot define its sentences against a semantic base (though, of course, it has =
one).3. =C2=A0The descriptions of languages used in the discussion of SWH a=
re those of surface phenomena as described in the first half of the 20th ce=
ntury and bear very little relation to what a linguist might do today (one =
would hope). In particular, all sentences of all languages have the same so=
rt of underlying representation and differ only in the selection of transfo=
rmation used to get to them, so the SAE etc. classifications, have no profo=
und reality. =C2=A0Nor do they reflect different ways of viewing the world,=
 as revealed in non-linguistic tests. =C2=A04. =C2=A0As noted, Nyaya Sanskr=
it is as formal a language as FOPL, just written in Sanskrit words not non-=
linguistic symbols. Spoken FOPL is in English (etc.) words but not the less=
 formal for that. Nyaya could be symboized in a HOIL fairly easily, I think=
 (I stopped that dissertation before I got that far, alas), so could be enf=
olded in Lojban, if Lojban were actually based on HOIL (or even a suitably =
extended version of FOPL).=C2=A05. =C2=A0I confess that, aside from constan=
tly fiddling with minutiae, I have no idea what reformers have as a vision =
for Lojban 2.0 or whatever. =C2=A0Does it still aim at the old goals, has i=
t dropped some, has it added others, is it totally different? Of course, ov=
er the years even the goals of the CLL fundamentalists have become increasi=
ngly less clear as even they diddle with this cmavo or that, even this. sel=
ma=E2=80=99o or that. =C2=A0All ultimately to no particularly interesting p=
oint, so far as I can see from what is floating around now. =C2=A0
    On Sunday, November 12, 2017, 6:15:37 AM CST, Martin Bays <mbays@sdf.or=
g> wrote: =20
=20
 * Sunday, 2017-11-12 at 12:55 +0100 - Ilmen <ilmen.pokebip@gmail.com>:

> Incidentally, there is a work-in-progress piece of software that aim to
> translate back and forth between Lojban and a custom logical notation ; t=
he
> project is called Tersmu: https://gitorious.org/tersmu/tersmu/

I should probably clarify that work on it isn't really in progress any
more, at least not by its original author (me). I'll try to maintain
it, but I can't imagine getting back to working on it seriously any
year soon. So I encourage anyone interested in developing the project
further to fork it.

